# ── CRM backend (WarriorCRM) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# The lead form posts to /api/lead, which forwards leads to your CRM
# server-side — the CRM credentials are never exposed to the browser.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local dev, and set the same vars in
# Vercel ▸ Project ▸ Settings ▸ Environment Variables for production.

# ── Option 1 (preferred): WarriorCRM via Supabase ────────────────────────
# Posts straight into the CRM's `public_leads` queue, which the CRM drains
# when you open it. Takes priority over CRM_WEBHOOK_URL below.
#
# The publishable key is frontend-safe by design: the CRM's row-level
# security lets it INSERT into public_leads ONLY — it cannot read any CRM data.
WARRIORCRM_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
WARRIORCRM_SUPABASE_KEY=your-supabase-publishable-key

# ── Option 2 (fallback): generic webhook ─────────────────────────────────
# Used only when the two WARRIORCRM_* vars above are not set.
# Your CRM's lead-intake endpoint (POST, accepts JSON).
CRM_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional: bearer token / API key sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>`.
# Leave blank if your endpoint doesn't need auth.
CRM_API_KEY=
